# Kitty is the terminal frontend; herdr owns panes, tabs, and persistence.

# A window is a plain login shell for the duration of the multiplexer trial.
#
# Zellij needed `shell zjshell` because a Zellij session is per-window: without a
# wrapper putting one there, a window had no multiplexer and no persistence.
# herdr inverts that — one server, already running as a systemd user unit, that
# `herdr` attaches to. There is nothing for a window to arrange, so it does not
# try, and windows that are not the herdr window stay ordinary terminals.
#
# `.` means the login shell from SHELL or /etc/passwd, run as a login shell,
# which is what makes ~/.bash_env's PATH available — the same reason
# Ctrl+Shift+Y's `bash -l` below spells it out.
#
# Reverting to Zellij is this one line: {{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.local/bin/zjshell
shell .

font_family JetBrainsMono Nerd Font Mono
font_size 10.5

cursor_shape block
cursor_blink_interval 0
scrollback_lines 10000
wheel_scroll_multiplier 3.0

window_padding_width 2
remember_window_size yes
initial_window_width 140c
initial_window_height 42c
tab_bar_min_tabs 2

enable_audio_bell no
allow_remote_control no
shell_integration enabled

# Zellij owns persistence, so closing a window only detaches the client. Nothing
# is lost, and the "it is running: ..." prompt is pure friction.
confirm_os_window_close 0

# An ordinary new window is a fresh single-pane session. These two open a window
# at the workspace picker instead, for attaching to an existing project. Either
# way the second layer is a Zellij session, never Kitty panes or tabs.
map ctrl+shift+enter launch --type=os-window --cwd=current zj
map ctrl+shift+t launch --type=os-window --cwd=current zj

# Deliberately NO F-key bindings here, and this is load-bearing rather than an
# omission. F2/F3/F4 (new tab, previous tab, next tab) belong to Zellij's bare
# function-key layer, and Kitty swallows a mapped key before any application in
# the window sees it. Binding them here does not shadow Zellij's versions — it
# deletes them, silently, with the tab bar still drawn and the keys simply dead.
# (Found the hard way when a trialled multiplexer bound all three here, which
# made it and Zellij mutually exclusive rather than merely both-installed.)

# The deliberately un-multiplexed window, and the only one on this machine.
#
# This mapping predates the herdr trial, during which `shell` is a plain login
# shell and so every window is already un-multiplexed. It is kept because the
# reasoning outlives the trial: multiplex at exactly one end, and for a remote
# host that end is the remote one, because that is where persistence across a
# dropped connection has to live. A detach exists for when nesting happens anyway,
# but the better answer is not to nest — multiplex at exactly one end, and for a
# remote host that end is the remote one, because that is where persistence
# across a dropped connection actually has to live.
#
# So: open this window, SSH from it, and the remote Zellij is the only Zellij in
# the stack. Every key, the mouse, the clipboard, and the scrollback belong to it
# unambiguously. The cost is that this window has no local splitting — use
# another window, which is what `confirm_os_window_close 0` makes cheap.
#
# `bash -l` rather than zjshell: `launch` overrides the configured shell, and a
# login shell is what makes ~/.bash_env's PATH available here.
map ctrl+shift+y launch --type=os-window --cwd=current bash -l

# The same window, but going straight to a host: an fzf picker over ~/.ssh/config
# and the `ssh` lines in history, which then `exec`s, so the remote is the
# window's own process and ending it closes the window.
#
# Ctrl+Shift+Y plus a remembered hostname is two steps, and the two-step version
# of the right answer loses to the one-step version of the wrong one — SSHing from
# an ordinary pane, which nests. This makes not nesting the cheaper habit.
#
# Displaces Kitty's start_resizing_window, which is meaningless here: Zellij owns
# panes and tabs, so Kitty's own layout keys have nothing to act on.
map ctrl+shift+r launch --type=os-window --cwd=current {{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.local/bin/sshz
